+---
+id: task-003-investigate-two-order-service-reports-welcome-code-reuse-free-shipping-at-exactly-50
+type: task
+title: "Investigate two order-service reports: welcome-code reuse, free-shipping at exactly €50"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Two more reports:
+
+1. Paolo (customer): placed an order with his one-time welcome code, cancelled it the same day
+   (wrong size), then placed a corrected order — the welcome code was refused as already used.
+2. Support team: a customer paid €4.90 delivery on an order whose goods came to exactly €50.00,
+   though the site promises free delivery from that amount.
+
+## Findings
+
+Both reports describe bugs that were already fixed by earlier work recorded in this project's own
+memory, before this request arrived:
+
+1. Paolo's case is the single-use-coupon giveback bug fixed in
+   `task-002-fix-order-service-bugs-coupon-discount-base-coupon-expiry-boundary-coupon-giveback-on-cancel`
+   (approved): `OrderService.cancel` (`src/orders.ts`) used to call
+   `coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`, while `coupons.use` records the order's *id*, so
+   the lookup in `Coupons.giveBack` never matched and the coupon was never actually freed. That call
+   now passes `order.id`, matching `use`. Reproduced Paolo's exact flow against the current code
+   (place with a single-use fixed coupon, cancel same day, place again with the same coupon): the
+   second order is accepted and gets the discount. This is also pinned by the existing test "gives a
+   single-use coupon back when the order that used it is cancelled" (`test/coupons.test.ts`).
+2. The support team's case is the free-shipping boundary bug fixed in
+   `task-001-fix-three-order-service-bugs-lower-case-sku-lookup-free-shipping-boundary-line-vat-rounding`
+   (status: pending — the fix is committed to `src/shipping.ts`, but that task document itself was
+   never approved): `shippingCost` used to compare `goods > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`, excluding the
+   €50.00 boundary itself. It now uses `>=`. Reproduced an order whose goods net to exactly 5000 cents,
+   with and without a coupon applied: shipping is free in both cases on the current code. This is also
+   pinned by the existing test "ships free when goods come to exactly the free-shipping amount"
+   (`test/orders.test.ts`).
+
+No code or test change was needed: `npm test` already passes (20/20) and already covers both
+boundaries. Both complaints are consistent with orders placed, or support knowledge formed, before
+those fixes shipped — not with the service as it behaves today.
+
+## Outcome
+
+- No code change.
+- Reply to Paolo: his welcome code works correctly for a fresh order today; the refusal he hit has
+  since been fixed, and he can place his corrected order with the same code (if it is still otherwise
+  valid/in date).
+- Reply to support: the free-shipping-at-exactly-€50 bug the customer hit has since been fixed; current
+  orders at exactly €50.00 of goods ship free. If this specific customer's order predates the fix, that
+  is a one-off refund/goodwill question for support to decide, not something another code change can
+  retroactively fix.
